   "evidence": "Line 78: `exact fun h1 \u21a6 closure_minimal (coe_subset_nonunits hJ) hU.isClosed_compl h1 isUnit_one`. Lines 86-87: `exact fun h1 \u21a6 closure_minimal (coe_subset_nonunits h\ud835\udd2a.ne_top) hU.isClosed_compl h1 isUnit_one`. Mathlib `Ideal.closure` (Topology/Algebra/Ring/Ideal.lean:30) has carrier `closure I`, the same set as `Submodule.topologicalClosure`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/Ring/MaximalIdeals.lean",
   "fix": "Add a semiring lemma, e.g. `Ideal.topologicalClosure_ne_top_of_isOpen_isUnit [Semiring A] [IsTopologicalSemiring A] (hU) (hJ : J \u2260 \u22a4) : J.topologicalClosure \u2260 \u22a4` (or the set-level `closure (J : Set A) \u2286 nonunits A`). Prove the ring-level `closure_ne_top_of_isOpen_isUnit` and the `hne` step from it, via `Ideal.coe_closure` / `SetLike.coe_injective` for the ring version.",
   "issue": "The `have hne : \ud835\udd2a.topologicalClosure \u2260 \u22a4` block (lines 84-87) repeats the proof of `Ideal.closure_ne_top_of_isOpen_isUnit` (lines 77-78): `rw [Ideal.ne_top_iff_one]; exact fun h1 \u21a6 closure_minimal (coe_subset_nonunits _) hU.isClosed_compl h1 isUnit_one`. Only the closure wrapper differs. So the key fact, 'the closure of a proper ideal of a topological semiring with open units avoids the units', has no name of its own, and the code now holds two copies of it.",
   "line": 84
  }
 ],
